1. OVERVIEW

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Automated Windows Printer Troubleshooter GUI is an enterprise-grade utility 

written in Python that automates the diagnosis and resolution of common Windows 

print spooler and print queue errors. It features a modern desktop graphical 

user interface (GUI) built with Python's native Tkinter framework and executes 

an underlying multi-step PowerShell troubleshooting engine.



1.1. Key Capabilities

* Automatic Network Discovery: Automatically enumerates installed network 

  printers, resolves their IP addresses or hostnames, and validates network 

  reachability via ping tests.

* Queue Inspection: Inspects active print jobs across all connected printers 

  and displays stuck documents.

* Service Management: Safely stops the Windows Print Spooler service (spooler) 

  using native service control routines.

* Spool Directory Purge: Unlocks and purges corrupted shadow (.shd) and spool 

  (.spl) files located in C:\Windows\System32\spool\PRINTERS.

* Automatic Spooler Restart: Restarts the Print Spooler service and confirms 

  operational health.

* Final Queue Verification: Verifies that print queues have been successfully 

  cleared and are ready to receive new print jobs.

* Auto-Elevation (UAC): Automatically requests Administrator privileges if 

  launched by an unelevated user.

* Non-Blocking Multithreaded Architecture: Runs diagnostics on a dedicated 

  worker thread to keep the user interface responsive and prevent "Not 

  Responding" states.





2. PREREQUISITES & SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Before setting up and running the application, ensure your environment meets the 

following technical specifications:



* Operating System   : Windows 10 or Windows 11 (64-bit recommended)

* Python Version     : Python 3.8, 3.9, 3.10, 3.11, or 3.12

* Standard Libraries : tkinter, ctypes, subprocess, threading, os, sys 

                       (All bundled with standard Windows Python installations)

* User Privileges    : Administrative privileges (required to stop/start 

                       Windows services and purge system directories)

* PowerShell         : Windows PowerShell 5.1 or later (pre-installed on 

                       Windows 10 and 11)





